    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="0938" n="804" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg804"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Moscow Embassy Files—897.6 Berlin Route</note>
                <head>No. 534<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Soviet Assistant Foreign
                        Commissar</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Vyshinsky</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-11">July 11, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Acknowledging receipt of
                    your letter of July 7<anchor n="1" xml:id="d534-f1"/> concerning the
                    establishment in Berlin of a civil airlines connection served by American and
                    Soviet airplanes, I must remind you that in our conversation of June 15 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] I called your attention to the fact that
                    practically speaking there has already been considerable improvement in air
                    communications over the given route and that I recognize the importance of this
                    matter, but I do not believe that at the present time this question is
                    sufficiently prepared for discussion in substance. As to the future, I can
                    inform you only upon receipt of instructions from the Soviet Government.</p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. 
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vyshinski</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
